\label{s2}
The mapping $f\mapsto Tf$ is unitary from de Branges - Rovnyak
space $H(s_0)$ onto $H(s)$.

A reproducing kernel Hilbert space $H$ of functions in $\mathcal{O}$ is of
the form $H=H(s)$ for some $s\in T\mathscr{S}$ if and only if
\begin{enumerate}
\item $H$ is $\partial$-invariant;
\item for every $f\in H$
$$\|\partial f\|_H^2\leq\|f\|_H^2-|f(0)|^2.$$
\end{enumerate}

\label{s5}
Tne following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item A function $f\in T\mathcal{O}$ is ${\lozenge}$-rational in the
sense that  for some  polynomial $p(z)$, not vanishing at the
origin, $p{\lozenge} f$ is also a polynomial.
\item $f(z)$ is of the form
$$f(z)=D+\int_0^zCe^{tA}Bdt$$ with $A,B,C,D$ - matrices of suitable dimensions;
\item the columns  of $\partial f$ belong to a finite-dimensional $\partial$-invariant space.
\end{enumerate}

A reproducing kernel Hilbert space $H$ of expandable functions is
of the form $H=H(s)$ for some $s\in VT\mathscr{S}$ if and only if
\begin{enumerate}
\item $H$ is $\delta_x$-invariant;
\item for every $f\in H$
$$\|\delta_x f\|_H^2\leq\|f\|_H^2-|f(0,0)|^2.$$
\end{enumerate}
